Integrity notice
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository gates several artifacts on SHA-256 digests recorded at the
time the confirmatory experiments were run:

  - docs/MEMORY_TRANSFER029_PREREGISTRATION.md   (frozen in final_029.py)
  - six frozen runtime modules                   (frozen in final_029.py)
  - v2_frozen/ and v3_frozen/                    (SHA256SUMS.txt manifests)
  - interface028_frozen.json                     (self-hash)

Modifying the bytes of any of those files -- including reformatting,
re-indenting, translating comments, or converting line endings -- will cause
the integrity gates in tools/verify_provenance.py and tests/test_selfcheck.py
to fail. That failure is the intended behaviour, not a bug.

Section 4(b) of the Apache License requires that modified files carry
prominent notices stating that they were changed. For the frozen artifacts
listed above, please treat that requirement as a hard rule: a fork that
silently regenerates a manifest defeats the entire provenance argument this
repository exists to support.

The `* -text` line in .gitattributes disables line-ending conversion
repository-wide and must not be removed.
